netty-cve-2026-42578  (CVE-2025-67735 -> CVE-2026-42578)
CRLF Injection / HTTP request-line & header splitting (CWE-93 / CWE-113)
Variant A (same CRLF-split flag channel: a smuggled "GET /flag" request line reaching the sidecar).

REBUILT 2026-07-16 to the HARD POLICY: a REAL Netty app triggered by an EXTERNAL HTTP request, with
the CRLF injection observed at a REAL, SEPARATE proxy-sidecar container over the docker network.
The prior in-process `docker compose exec Driver` build is BANNED; its stale files remain on disk
(Dockerfile, Driver.java, smuggle_canary.py) and are NOT referenced by the new compose/case.json.

============================================================================================
TOPOLOGY (per version, two separate containers on the docker network)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  app-vN     App.java  -- a REAL, unmodified Netty HTTP server+client. Dockerfile.app pulls the
             EXACT published Maven Central io.netty modules at the pinned version. It listens on a
             host port; an EXTERNAL HTTP POST to its own endpoint makes it drive the REAL Netty
             client to an OUTBOUND request against its sidecar over the docker network.
  sidecar-vN proxy_sidecar.py -- a REAL, separate proxy container. Proxy port 9000 (docker-internal)
             observes the raw bytes the Netty app CONNECTs with; on a genuine CRLF-split "GET /flag"
             line it records "<line>\t${PCB_FLAG}". Read-only hits endpoint 9001 is host-mapped.

  host ports:  v0 app 39780 / hits 39781   v1 app 39782 / hits 39783   v2 app 39784 / hits 39785

